  "body": "Branch `fn-paged-kv-pool` `336cb3f7`. It is #1156's `ce5b78d7`, then #1169 (`85aeb4bf`, the same change as `f23b5ab5`), then this change. It uses #1156's\n`served()` and host plan.\n\n## What this changes\n\n`TF_FLASHNEXT_KV_PAGES=n` is off by default; n must be a multiple of 4. One stream keeps its own caches. Every other\nstream takes a pool lane (`cuda_kv_lanes.zig`), which holds only its page table while idle:\n\n- Its attention caches are n-position pages of one arena, enough for its prompt, its reply and a drafted window. With\n  the MTP head a page holds the head's cache too, as the layer after the model's.\n- Its DeltaNet states, convolution and n-gram tails and the head's buffers (window streams, scores, saved rows, spare\n  states; `Draft.initIn`) are one run of consecutive pool pages, claimed when the stream opens (`Pool.claimRun`) and\n  given back when it closes. Only addresses move.\n\nThe host plans the pool from `Loaded.layout` (fixed: the table and image rows; pages a token; the run) and admits through\n`fits`. A request waits (`LaneMemory`) when no lane, pages or run is free. A lane's pages and run go back once the\nengine's stream drains. Prompt-cache copies of the head's cache follow its pages. The layout is made after the head is\nloaded, so the run covers every buffer the head maps (`initIn` refuses a short run).\n\n`TF_FLASHNEXT_KV_PAGES_ALL=1` puts every stream on pages, for checks. Two ranks, `--slide` and a captured set refuse\nthe variable.\n\n## Receipt\n\n- At n=256, `--parallel 4 --context 40960`, MTP: \"3 more taking 594 pages of 256 rows (4.36 GiB) as they need them,\n  0 MiB fixed each\". Before the run change each lane held 369 MiB from load (states, head cache and buffers).\n- With MTP drafts:\n  - concurrent == alone 4/4 and serial 1/1, outputs equal to contiguous;\n  - drafted == plain 8/8, concurrent == solo 8/8, resumed == fresh (7,147 tokens), all equal to contiguous.\n- Pages only (`--parallel 5`, 4 lanes, 792 pages, 8 requests, some waiting): the same bytes, and a kept state with its\n  head cache restored into a lane.\n- Without drafts, with the states in runs: see Gotchas (within noise of contiguous, bytes equal).\n- Tests: full `zig build test -Dnvcc=/usr/local/cuda/bin/nvcc` exit 0 (the admission test sets the new field), fmt\n  clean, lean 0 new findings; `kernel-contract` 85/85, 7 controls red.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- **Stacked on #1156 and on #1169:** the diff against `main` includes #1156's qwen commits up to `ce5b78d7`, and the page-table change, until those land. Only the last commit is this change.\n- **Off by default** (`TF_FLASHNEXT_KV_PAGES`). Two ranks, `--slide` and captured sets refuse it.\n- **No-drafts speed with the states in runs:** within noise of contiguous. These are two rounds of fresh server starts on this tree, with replies byte-identical to contiguous (code/chat tok/s):\n  - c=1: contiguous 23.44/23.13 and 23.71/23.73; pool on 23.57/23.55 and 23.55/23.55; pages only 23.60/23.50 and 23.64/23.48.\n  - c=4: contiguous 64.7/64.7 and 66.0/64.9; pool on 65.4/64.9 and 66.0/65.5; pages only 65.8/65.3 and 65.0/64.2.\n- **Waits:** in pages-only mode with more requests than lanes, a waiting request can wait several seconds (up to 9.5 s seen with 8 requests on 4 lanes).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Every token still goes through the lane rounds.\n- [x] Drafted == plain, resumed == fresh, concurrent == solo, as measured above.\n- [x] No precision traded for speed. The bits do not change.\n- [x] New and changed kernels are registered with the kernel contract, with red controls.\n- [x] Prompt processing is no slower than the last release (contiguous within main's spread).\n- [x] Platforms: CUDA on GB10 (sm_121), one rank; other SMs through recorded compiles; no Metal change.\n- [x] Comments are one line. No measurements or history in the source (lean check 0 new).\n- [x] No personal data, machine names, internal hosts or local paths. No AI attribution lines.\n\n",
